From 5447eb3bc24cf126338f622064b72ee7a90965cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:27:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 112/121] net: phy: micrel: lan8814: disable EEE

The LAN8814 can enter 100BASE-TX EEE low power idle spuriously after the
cable is unplugged (errata module 24).  The PHY advertises EEE out of
reset, so two LAN8814s negotiate it even when neither MAC supports LPI,
since phylink only disables PHY EEE for MACs that implement the LPI ops.

Disable EEE at probe, the default in Microchip's PHY API.

Signed-off-by: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/micrel.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/micrel.c b/drivers/net/phy/micrel.c
index 7e20ccfec770..92daa60411d1 100644
--- a/drivers/net/phy/micrel.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/micrel.c
@@ -4745,6 +4745,11 @@ static int lan8814_probe(struct phy_device *phydev)
 	lan8814_clear_2psp_bit(phydev);
 	lan8814_update_meas_time(phydev);
 
+	/* Errata module 24: spurious LPI entry on cable unplug.  Keep EEE
+	 * off, as Microchip's PHY API does by default.
+	 */
+	phy_disable_eee(phydev);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
